smstools-http-api (2.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Address book (CONTACTS): vCards from a CardDAV address book (cached)
    or a file; contacts answer to nicknames, groups (categories), names,
    e-mail addresses and numbers.
  * Webhooks of type 'route': a received SMS goes by mail to the contacts
    named by its leading @tokens (default recipient otherwise); the mail
    comes from <number>@<sms domain>, so a reply becomes an SMS.
  * smstools-http-api-mail2sms: MTA pipe that sends a mail to
    <name or number>@<sms domain> as SMS (allowed senders only; mail from
    untrusted clients needs Received-SPF: pass).

 -- Mario Fetka <mario.fetka@gmail.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0100

smstools-http-api (2.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Webhooks of type 'email': mail events (e.g. received SMS) over SMTP,
    with the same queue and retries as the HTTP webhooks.

 -- Mario Fetka <mario.fetka@gmail.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0100

smstools-http-api (2.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Webhooks for smsd events: smstools-http-api-event (smsd eventhandler)
    queues RECEIVED/SENT/FAILED/REPORT/CALL events, the new
    smstools-http-api-webhooks service delivers them with retries
    (WEBHOOKS in settings.py; custom payload, e.g. Zabbix history.push).

 -- Mario Fetka <mario.fetka@gmail.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

